[16:50:43] ## What changed
[16:50:43] **The asset and the reference** (AC 1, 2)
[16:50:43] - `frontend/public/favicon.ico` — new, the documented replaceable file. A plain 32×32 neutral grey rounded square as a real binary ICO (4286 bytes, sha256 `bed9e566fb26…`): no base64 in source, no data URI, no image service, no generator script and no new dependency in the repo. The bytes came from a throwaway Node script kept *outside* the repository, so the project doesn't acquire an icon-generation step for a disposable placeholder.
[16:50:43] - `frontend/index.html:6` — one standard `<link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="%BASE_URL%favicon.ico" />`. `%BASE_URL%` is Vite's own base substitution, so the emitted href tracks the configured base exactly like the script/stylesheet URLs.
[16:50:43] **Instructions** (AC 3) — `README.md`, "Running locally" → "Browser favicon": exact path, expected `.ico` format (single 32×32, or 16/32/48 multi-size), overwrite-then-reload / `npm run build` steps, and the favicon-cache trap with three ways out. It says plainly the current file is a placeholder, "not intended as the project's final icon".
[16:50:43] **Verification** (AC 4) — new `frontend/scripts/favicon-browser-smoke.mjs` + `npm run smoke:favicon`.
[16:50:43] ## Tests run (in `frontend/`)
[16:50:43] - `npm run build` — clean; `dist/index.html` emits `href="/favicon.ico"` with no unresolved `%BASE_URL%`, and `dist/favicon.ico` is byte-identical to `public/favicon.ico`.
[16:50:43] - `npx vite build --base=/gw2/ --outDir dist-base-check` → `href="/gw2/favicon.ico"` beside `/gw2/assets/index-*.js`; temp dir removed.
[16:50:43] - `npm run smoke:favicon` — **PASSED, 7 steps** in real Chrome 152 on its own stub origin at `127.0.0.1:5186`: one icon link resolving to that origin, a real in-page request answered **HTTP 200 `image/x-icon`, 4286 bytes with the source file's sha256** (served by the origin, not from cache), those bytes **decoded to a 32×32 image**, all six destinations still opening, no `/api/` route involved, nothing off-origin, no page errors.
[16:50:43] - `npm run smoke:icons` — **PASSED, 10 steps**, unchanged (5 image requests, 17 same-origin), re-run because a new asset can break an existing request assertion. Chromium loads tab icons through its own loader, which Playwright reports in no script's request list — that's why the new check counts server-side hits rather than page request events.
[16:50:43] - Not run: `npm test` (the Vitest suite never loads `index.html`) and the other smoke scripts; CI is the full gate.
[16:50:43] Docs updated: `README.md` and `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.11 (file tree, new "Browser tab icon" paragraph, the "Not built yet" paragraph that claimed there is no favicon, one command row). Story file, `BACKLOG.md` and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` updated; `CURRENT_STORY.md` and `PROJECT_STATE.md` untouched.
[16:50:43] ## Two things worth your attention
[16:50:43] 1. The story cites `TARGET_ARCHITECTURE.md` §12.1 as authoritative for a "standard replaceable favicon asset", but §12.1 as written covers only item/recipe icon delivery and states no favicon rule — `Request-004`'s resolution note assumed it did. I followed the acceptance criteria (which are unambiguous) and invented no rule; whether §12.1 should gain that sentence is an architecture decision I left open, recorded in the Result and backlog entry.
[16:50:43] 2. The icon was verified from the built output against a controlled origin. Nothing serves `frontend/dist/` from the backend or a container today, so that path is unverified by design.
